  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IPLC land rights, forest protection and development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The impact of the project will be reduced loss of tropical forests, enhanced biodiversity conservation and improved well-being of IPLCs though community stewardship in supported areas. The project will directly support community-led protection of over 250,000 hectares of forest in DRC and Gabon through partnerships with eight local organisations (three in Gabon), in order to deliver three outcomes: 

Outcome 1: Improved tenure security and livelihoods for IPLCs
Outcome 2: Forest crimes and threats to IPLCs are effectively addressed and mitigated
Outcome 3: Governance framewoks for forests and IPLC rights are strengthened at local, national and international levels.</narrative>
  </description>
